<span data-as=3D"p">Routing workflows process inputs and then directs them =
to context-specific tasks. This allows you to define specialized flows for =
complex tasks. For example, a workflow built to answer product related ques=
tions might process the type of question first, and then route the request =
to specific processes for pricing, refunds, returns, etc.</span>
