<span data-as=3D"p">Orchestrator-worker workflows provide more flexibility =
and are often used when subtasks cannot be predefined the way they can with=
 <a href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/workflows-agent=
s#parallelization" class=3D"link">parallelization</a>. This is common with =
workflows that write code or need to update content across multiple files. =
For example, a workflow that needs to update installation instructions for =
multiple Python libraries across an unknown number of documents might use t=
his pattern.</span>
