<span data-as=3D"p">In evaluator-optimizer workflows, one LLM call creates =
a response and the other evaluates that response. If the evaluator or a <a =
class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/inte=
rrupts">human-in-the-loop</a> determines the response needs refinement, fee=
dback is provided and the response is recreated. This loop continues until =
an acceptable response is generated.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">Evaluator-optimizer workflows are commonly used when th=
ere=E2=80=99s particular success criteria for a task, but iteration is requ=
ired to meet that criteria. For example, there=E2=80=99s not always a perfe=
ct match when translating text between two languages. It might take a few i=
terations to generate a translation with the same meaning across the two la=
nguages.</span>
